# Reverse-engineering toolkit (xapk -> il2cpp dump -> config parser -> assets).
# Local-only: heavy tool binaries + game archives, never part of the published app.
reverseForge/

# Server-side infrastructure and its operator notes. Deployment config, not application code.
#
# WORTH KNOWING: `supabase/migrations/*.sql` is the definition of the live database, and once it is
# ignored here this is its only copy — no history, no backup. Keep it somewhere backed up.
#
# The client half of the feature stays tracked (src/services/clanApi.ts, the contexts, the Auth and
# Clan components, pushClient.ts, public/sw.js, the manifest): it ships in the bundle regardless, and
# dropping it would only break the build for anyone who clones the project.
supabase/
docs/
!docs/attack-timing.md

# ---- Local tooling and scratch output. Never application code, never shipped. ----
#
# The harness pages below drive the OCR readers from `reverseForge/` (ignored above) and are not
# build entries: vite builds `index.html` only, and nothing under `src/` imports them. A clone does
# not need them and the published site must not carry them. They stay on disk, just untracked.
/ocr-harness.html
/techtree_mapper.html
/src/harness/

# One-off probe pages and the image dumps they write.
__*probe*.html
*_probe.html
public/__*/

# Headless-browser screenshots and one-off measurement scripts, written beside the app while
# something is being checked. Nothing legitimate lives loose at the repo root.
/*.png
/.*.mjs
/*.tsv

